From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Ramsden <tomjramsden@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:16:03 +0000
Subject: guard-low-water: The GPU memory guard lets go of what has idled near
 the driver's low-water mark and names a slow game there

From about half of Metal's working set, IOGPUFamily's wired collector frees at every command buffer (kernel log: IOGPUCommandDescriptor::prepare FAILED To Free) and the game runs at about 10 fps: Ocarina of Time in Hyrule Field after 15 minutes on a 24 GB M4 Pro, 9.0-9.5 GB required. GUARD_SOFT (80% of half the working set): sharing entries idle for 1,800 submissions, spares and staging go every 120 frames. guard_low_tick (92%): a game under 40% of its best frame rate for three seconds is named in the log and to the front end (front_gpu_memory_low). DM_NVN_GUARD_SOFT_MB sets or turns off the levels; DM_NVN_RES_BALLAST grows a short run's set for the check. docs/reference/memory.md has the entry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
