+### The GPU driver frees at every command buffer from about half the working set
+
+- **Symptom:** a game that held 60 fps drops to about 10 over a few seconds and stays there, in slow motion, until a pause menu: GPU time per frame triples (15 to 35-50 ms) with the same draws, at a lower dynamic resolution, and `guest fence waits` take most of each long frame. No shader, upload or residency cost in the `[longframe]` lines, no thermal or power event. The kernel log (`/usr/bin/log show --predicate 'process == "kernel" AND eventMessage CONTAINS "IOGPUCommandDescriptor"'`) has thousands of `IOGPUCommandDescriptor::prepare(uint32_t) <dmhost> FAILED To Free, should return error: <0xE00002BE> total accelerator = … max = …` lines a minute for exactly that stretch. Now: `GPU memory guard: … past the driver's low-water mark … Saving and starting the game again empties it`, a toast and a note on the sidebar's Performance page.
+- **Cause:** IOGPUFamily's wired collector. Long before the working set (`max` in that line is `recommendedMaxWorkingSetSize`), once the process's wired GPU memory cannot be brought back under a mark near half of it, the driver tries to free at every command buffer it prepares and fails, as the residency set holds everything. Ocarina of Time (Switch 2) on a 24 GB M4 Pro (macOS 27.2, working set 18,186 MB): 6,843 such lines in the minute the game ran at 11-14 fps after 15 minutes of play, with 9.0-9.5 GB required by its command buffers (`requiredBytes` in the `preparedBytes != requiredBytes` lines the driver logs for this host throughout) and `total accelerator` between 9,136 and 10,206 MB; a burst of 717 at the session's only other GPU spike. It is the game's own memory, not the Mac's: with private buffers added to the set of a headless run of the same scene (`DM_NVN_RES_BALLAST`, 128 MB a second), the first refusal came at 8.5-8.9 GB in the set (`total accelerator` 9,450-9,569 MB) in three runs, one of them with another process holding 8 GB (memory pressure at warning, swap growing), and 60 fps turned to 9. Without the ballast the scene holds 5.7-6.5 GB and 60 fps with 16 GB held elsewhere. A plain Metal 3 program that used 17 GB of private textures in every command buffer logged no such line. Not measured: other Macs, other macOS versions, where the mark sits when the working set is smaller (the 16 GB Mac of [the entry below](#what-fills-a-switch-2-games-gpu-working-set-ocarina-of-time-on-an-ipad) ran with about 9.4 GB wired).
+- **Fix:** NXForge, `nvn_mtl.m`, Mac only. The guard has two levels under its own: from 80% of half the working set (`g_guard.soft`, 7,274 MB there) the submit thread lets go every 120 frames of what a long session leaves behind (`GUARD_SOFT` in `guard_evict`: sharing entries nothing holds and no lookup found for 1,800 submissions, re-upload spares, upload staging); from 92% of it (`g_guard.low`, 8,365 MB) a game that shows under 40% of its best frame rate for three seconds is named in the log and to the player (`guard_low_tick`, `front_gpu_memory_low`: an 8 second toast and a note on the sidebar's Performance page), at most every five minutes. `DM_NVN_GUARD_SOFT_MB=<MB>` sets the soft level (the low one 15% above it), `0` turns both off. This does not lower what the live scene needs: a set that is past the mark with nothing idle stays slow, and the note says what frees it. [Read marks that go with their next texture](rendering.md#area-loads-froze-late-in-a-session-as-read-marks-piled-up) (PR #2344) lowers what a long session accumulates.
+- **Check:** `make -C dm/gfx/tests GAME=<id> check_t_res_guard`: the two levels from the working set and from the switch, the soft level a level of its own, a soft pass keeping an entry idle for 16 submissions that the eviction level lets go. In the game: Ocarina of Time, Hyrule Field, headless, `DM_NVN_RES_BALLAST=128:70:1:6144`: the soft passes from 7,262 MB (28 idle entries, staging), the refusals from 12:01:14 at 8.6-9.0 GB required, the guard's line two seconds later at 9,377 MB with 11 frames a second against 62. Not checked: a long windowed session, how much the soft passes free in one (the headless scene has 29 idle entries), another Mac.
+- **Found on:** [The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time](../../dm/games/0400486024DEC000/README.md#memory) (Switch 2, `0400486024DEC000`, v131072).
+
 ### A pipeline archive on an external drive is read into memory
 
 - **Symptom:** `footprint` shows `Malloc Large` about the size of `pso_archive/` (the log's `pipeline archive …: N files, … MB`), resident or swapped for the whole run. `MallocStackLogging=1` with `malloc_history <pid> -allBySize` gives `newArchiveWithURL` → `MTL4ArchiveImpl::loadFromURL` → `LoaderGlobalState::loadFile` → `-[NSData initWithContentsOfFile:options:maxLength:error:]` → malloc.
